      "writtenOn": "2021-10-26T20:23:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if the shader could return it\u0027s implementation FP without worrying about disabling coverage as alpha and then change the condition on line 472 to be\n if (paintAlpha !\u003d 1.0f \u0026\u0026 !paintFP-\u003ecompatibleWithCoverageAsAlpha()) {\n \nIOW, does having the compatibleWithCoverageAsAlpha() also mean it\u0027s ok to pre-apply paint alpha rather than post-apply it? It seems like it should since that\u0027s what we do with coverage when we use the optimization. And then we\u0027d skip the extra alpha application of the shader and be able to batch opaque and non-opaque draws that share the same shader (and also slightly simplify the SkShader::asFragmentProcessor() implementations).",
      "parentUuid": "3e3f7f53_445f6f0f",
      "revId": "c92995dc722cfbd9a830c4bb91f1563bb1b62b0d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
